---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Sub-120ms Hard Real-Time Physical Actuation" activeNav="actuation">
  <div class="container-wide" style="padding-top: 28px;">

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.8rem;">
      <a href="/" style="color: var(--text-muted); text-decoration: none;">Platform</a>
      <span style="color: var(--border-medium);">/</span>
      <span style="color: var(--brand-primary); font-weight: 700;">Sub-120ms Actuation</span>
    </div>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <span class="top-tag"><span class="pulse-dot"></span> PILLAR 05: HARD REAL-TIME CONTROL</span>
        <span class="card-badge badge-danger">SUB-120ms DETERMINISTIC RELAYS</span>
        <span class="card-badge badge-safe">ZERO-FAIL SAFE ARCHITECTURE</span>
      </div>
      
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 14px; max-width: 960px; color: var(--text-primary);">
        Autonomous Physical Actuation: Sub-120ms Hard Real-Time Relay &amp; Siren Control
      </h1>
      
      <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 860px; line-height: 1.6;">
        Early warning without physical actuation is ineffective. WATCH-DOGS replaces human call-trees and manual lever operations with autonomous, optocoupled solid-state relays that trip high-decibel acoustic warning sirens, deploy motorized highway barricades, and open siphon drainage floodgates in under 120 milliseconds.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Chronometer Latency Breakdown Strip -->
    <div class="metric-grid" style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
      <div class="metric-box" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--brand-primary);">
        <div class="metric-value">64.0 ms</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Acoustic Siren Grid</div>
        <div class="metric-sub">130 dB Solid-State SSR Relay Trip</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-box" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--status-safe);">
        <div class="metric-value">92.0 ms</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Solenoid Siphon Gate</div>
        <div class="metric-sub">24V High-Current Inductive Valve</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-box" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--status-warning);">
        <div class="metric-value">108.0 ms</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Highway Boom Barricade</div>
        <div class="metric-sub">Galvanically Isolated Motor Drive</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-box" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--status-danger);">
        <div class="metric-value">&lt; 120 ms</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Total Worst-Case Budget</div>
        <div class="metric-sub">Guaranteed by Hard Real-Time FSM</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Physical Hardware Actuation Subsystem Gallery with User Optocoupler Photo -->
    <h2 class="section-title">Physical Hardware Actuation Subsystems</h2>

    <div class="bento-grid" style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
      <div class="bento-card col-6" style="padding: 0; overflow: hidden; border-top: 4px solid var(--brand-primary);">
        <div style="height: 180px; background: #ffffff; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
          <img src="/iMAGES/PC817_4-Channel_Optocoupler_Isolation_Module_1.webp" alt="PC817 4-Channel Optocoupler Module" style="max-height: 100%; max-width: 100%; object-fit: contain;" />
        </div>
        <div style="padding: 16px;">
          <span class="card-badge badge-brand" style="font-size: 0.70rem;">GALVANIC SOLID-STATE TRIP</span>
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 800; margin: 4px 0 6px;">PC817 4-Channel Optocoupled Relay Board</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">Optically isolates the low-voltage 3.3V ESP32 microcontroller logic from high-voltage 24V/230V siren horns and heavy motorized barrier drivers, preventing inductive voltage spikes from damaging the compute core.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bento-card col-6" style="padding: 0; overflow: hidden; border-top: 4px solid var(--status-safe);">
        <div style="height: 180px; background: #ffffff; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
          <img src="/iMAGES/CN3791-12V-MPPT-Solar-Charger-Module-6.png" alt="CN3791 MPPT Solar Charger" style="max-height: 100%; max-width: 100%; object-fit: contain;" />
        </div>
        <div style="padding: 16px;">
          <span class="card-badge badge-safe" style="font-size: 0.70rem;">AUTONOMOUS POWER HARVESTING</span>
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 800; margin: 4px 0 6px;">CN3791 MPPT Solar Charging Controller</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">Maintains high-efficiency Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) charging for the 3.2V LiFePO4 battery pack, ensuring continuous actuation readiness even after 80+ days of monsoon cloud cover.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 5-State Finite State Machine (FSM) Diagram -->
    <div class="bento-card col-12" style="border-left: 5px solid var(--status-danger); margin-bottom: 36px; padding: 24px;">
      <div class="card-header" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
        <div>
          <span class="card-badge badge-danger">FINITE STATE MACHINE ARCHITECTURE</span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary); margin-top: 4px;">5-State Deterministic Disaster Actuation Engine</h2>
        </div>
        <span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Fail-Safe Watchdog Timer: 250ms</span>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        State transitions are strictly non-blocking. When <code>STATE 3: CODE RED</code> is triggered, the kernel executes direct memory-mapped register writes to the GPIO subsystem, bypassing userspace overhead to fire physical optocouplers in &lt;1ms.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f8fafc 0%, #edf2f7 100%); border: 1.5px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 28px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 8px;">Explore Dynamic Evacuation &amp; Road Rerouting Intelligence</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 650px; margin: 0 auto 20px;">
        See how WATCH-DOGS continuously recalculates escape vectors around mudslide debris and flooded bridges in real time.
      </p>
      <a href="/evacuation" class="btn btn-primary">Proceed to Evacuation Intelligence &rarr;</a>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
